; The rewriter's suite, and a directory of its own rather than a stanza in
; test/. It is the one place in this repository preprocessed by ppx_camlcast,
; and the preprocessing has to reach exactly it: a description compiled with
; the rewriter carries a position and one compiled without it does not, and
; every other suite asserts on the second of those.
;
; The directory is what makes `dune build @check` work -- the alias merlin and
; the language server build. Dune's check context is per directory: a stanza
; here whose (libraries) differ from its neighbours' gets those neighbours'
; instead, and the modules this suite names stop resolving under @check while
; an ordinary `dune build` is perfectly happy. Alone in a directory it has its
; own context and the question does not arise.
;
; It links camlcast_vocabulary, which is where the rewriter keeps the names it
; wraps, so that this suite reads that list rather than a copy of it. A copy is
; the thing this suite exists to prevent.
;
; The action passes %{profile} in, and that is load-bearing rather than
; decorative. Whether the rewriter put positions on this file is something the
; rewriter can report about itself, and a test believing that report proves
; only that it is self-consistent: were CAMLCAST_POSITIONS to reach a release
; build, the report and the positions would both flip and the suite would pass
; while the thing it guards had failed. The profile comes from dune instead, so
; the expectation and the fact have separate sources.

(tests
 (names test_ppx)
 (modules test_ppx)
 (package camlcast)
 (deps ../../lib/p.mli)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_camlcast))
 (action
  (setenv
   CAMLCAST_PROFILE
   %{profile}
   (run %{test})))
 (libraries camlcast camlcast_vocabulary alcotest))
